# Normalise everything to LF in the repo AND in the working copy.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The shell scripts here get uploaded to Linux boxes, and a
# CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails with a syntax error pointing at a line far from
# anything you edited — see content-factory/memory/lesson_windows_experiment_harness.md,
# which exists because that trap cost a real experiment run.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
